# Storage layout

Every stored file, in Azure blobs and in local file storage, uses this path and nothing else:

```text
{orgId}/{officeName}/{category}/{file}
{orgId}/{officeName}/{category}/{propertyCode}/{file}
```

Pictures use the second form. `propertyCode` is required for listings, inspection photos, and any other property picture.

## Hard rule

**Nothing is ever stored at the root of an org.** The first child under `{orgId}` is always an office name. Do not put a file, a category, or a property folder directly under the org.

- Do not skip the office segment.
- Do not flatten office, category, and property into one folder (`denver-listings-bar0903`).
- Do not pass `office/listings/code` or `office/inspection/code` through as a single office name.
- A missing office uses the `global` office folder. It does not write at the org root.
- Keep spaces in the office name. Do not replace a space with a hyphen (`las vegas`, not `las-vegas`).

## Examples

```text
{orgId}/denver/listings/bar0903/photo.jpg
{orgId}/denver/inspection/bar0903/photo.jpg
{orgId}/denver/profiles/avatar.jpg
{orgId}/denver/logos/logo.png
{orgId}/global/profiles/avatar.jpg
```

```text
{orgId}/photo.jpg
{orgId}/listings/bar0903/photo.jpg
{orgId}/denver-listings-bar0903/photo.jpg
```
